476 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(The purpose of this assessment is to help your manager understand the things you value here at Cortland. Research has shown that employees who think there is a good balance between what they give to and what they get from their jobs are more likely to be committed to their work and their organization.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

477 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E( These associates feel a stronger sense of ownership because they believe that they and their employer are committed to each other\220s success. Ownership is defined as the state in which employees feel fully engaged in and responsible for their work and its impact on the organization\220s success.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

478 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(This assessment asks you to rate the importance of 25 research-based factors related to ownership. While all of the factors are significant influencers of employee commitment, managers need to know which of them are most important to each individual associate.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

479 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(In an upcoming session called Ownership, your manager will be analyzing the assessments that you and others in your work group complete in order to identify ways to encourage and sustain employees\220 ownership.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

480 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(You are asked only to provide information about how important each factor is to you. After the session, your manager will be following up with you to discuss your assessment responses, as well as your views on how well the organization is doing on those factors you value most. Be assured that, although your manager will be looking at your responses, they will not be shared with anyone else at the session.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

481 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(As you complete the assessment, try to distinguish those factors that matter most to you \(those that most affect your commitment and sense of ownership\)\204rather than rate all of them as important to a great or very great extent. In other words, communicate your priorities clearly in your ratings. Rate those factors that are less important to you \(those that do not really influence your commitment to your job or your organization at present\) as important to a small extent or not at all important. It is most valuable for your manager to know the \215critical few\216 factors that are most important to you at present.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

482 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 117 0 R/T(INSTRUCTIONS)/E(INSTRUCTIONS)/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Use the scale at the upper right on the assessment to indicate the importance of each of the factors related to ownership. How important is each? \(Consider which ones most affect your commitment to your job and most influence your decision to stay with your organization. Even if all the factors appear somewhat important, indicate the ones that are most important to you at present.\))/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Write your name at the top of the assessment and return it to your manager by the date he or she has indicated.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

